Ladybird now limits a replaced flex item’s automatic inline
contribution by its min-height and max-height transferred through its
aspect ratio, as all three engines do for intrinsic sizes. Gecko’s
nsLayoutUtils::IntrinsicForAxis() clamps the intrinsic inline size by
the transferred max and min block sizes. WebKit’s RenderReplaced::
computeIntrinsicSizesConstrainedByTransferredMinMaxSizes() constrains
the natural size the same way. And Blink sizes a replaced item through
ComputeReplacedSize(), which applies the transferred min/max sizes.
